Graph image: keep the Ubuntu 24.04 CUDA base's system Python installable

Upstream's apps/graph/Dockerfile installs python3.12 from apt in its
base-cuda stage, but the compose file pins that stage to
nvidia/cuda:12.1.0-runtime-ubuntu22.04, and jammy has no python3.12
package, so `BUILD_TYPE=cuda` cannot build at pin e5488b2a (KB-68).
docker/interp/neuronpedia.override.yaml moves the stage to an Ubuntu
24.04 base that has the package. Noble marks its system Python as
externally managed (PEP 668), which would refuse the Dockerfile's
`pip install poetry` and poetry's install into system site-packages
(POETRY_VIRTUALENVS_CREATE=false). This removes the marker in the
same RUN. On 22.04 the file does not exist and the line is a no-op,
so upstream's defaults are unchanged.

Upstream tracking: not yet filed. Delete this patch at the pin bump
that carries an upstream fix for the cuda base.

diff --git a/apps/graph/Dockerfile b/apps/graph/Dockerfile
index 453b174..894781e 100644
--- a/apps/graph/Dockerfile
+++ b/apps/graph/Dockerfile
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@ RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
     python3-pip \
     python3.12-venv \
     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
-    && ln -sf /usr/bin/python3.12 /usr/bin/python
+    && ln -sf /usr/bin/python3.12 /usr/bin/python \
+    && rm -f /usr/lib/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED
 
 # Main build stage
 FROM base-${BUILD_TYPE:-nocuda} AS final
